[C2] PASS for a linear rate law the step (I/dt - N J) dc = N rate is one backward-Euler step: dc = [-0.552631578947  0.552631578947], backward Euler [-0.552631578947  0.552631578947]
[C3] PASS one step moves toward equilibrium by 1/(1 + dt (k_f + k_b)) and never past it, for any dt: max deviation from the contraction factor / (1e-14 cond) = 0.01 over dt in [1e-3, 1e6]
[C4] PASS a mass-balanced reaction changes the species densities with zero net mass: max |sum_n mu_n dc_n| / max|mu_n dc_n| = 2.1e-15 over 100 random steps
[C5] PASS particles c V_m/(pi d^3/6) times 2 pi d D zeta = Gamma c zeta: Gamma = 12 D V_m / d_p^2 (sympy)
